    "b-agent-discovery-decision-7": {
      "id": "b-agent-discovery-decision-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "the kernel discovers a bundle's tools on disk by filename convention — a flat "
        },
        {
          "insert": "tools.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " checked before a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "tools/index.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " folder entry, exporting a register function as the default export or under the name "
        },
        {
          "insert": "tools",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — and this bundle uses the folder form only: a flat "
        },
        {
          "insert": "tools.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " must never exist beside "
        },
        {
          "insert": "catalog/layout-editor/tools/",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/catalog/layout-editor/tools",
              "label": "catalog/layout-editor/tools/"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", because the file form is checked first and would silently shadow the folder — the surface would be wrong with no error, no warning."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-agent-discovery-why-8": {
      "id": "b-agent-discovery-why-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "the rejected alternative was configured registration (a manifest field naming the entry point); the layout is the configuration, and the shadow ban is absolute because the failure mode is silent."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-agent-discovery-applies-9": {
      "id": "b-agent-discovery-applies-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "catalog/layout-editor/tools/",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/catalog/layout-editor/tools",
              "label": "catalog/layout-editor/tools/"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — including every future bundle, which uses one form and keeps the other absent."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-agent-static-reg-decision-10": {
      "id": "b-agent-static-reg-decision-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "registration is side-effect-free and constructible from static data alone — it reads descriptors and declares tools, touching no session, draft, or render — because registry boot dry-runs it with a stub registrar and no runtime at all, to harvest the allowlist before any spawn exists; each tool's execute defers the runtime check to call time via "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/canvas-agent/src/catalog/layout-editor/tools/runtime.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/catalog/layout-editor/tools/runtime.ts",
              "symbol": "requireRuntime"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-agent-static-reg-why-11": {
      "id": "b-agent-static-reg-why-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "the rejected alternative was checking for a bound runtime at registration, which would fail every boot — no session exists at boot — and any registration side effect would fire during the harvest."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-agent-static-reg-applies-12": {
      "id": "b-agent-static-reg-applies-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "catalog/layout-editor/tools/index.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/catalog/layout-editor/tools/index.ts",
              "label": "catalog/layout-editor/tools/index.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — including every future tool, whose declaration stays inert and whose execute calls "
        },
        {
          "insert": "requireRuntime",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-agent-binding-decision-13": {
      "id": "b-agent-binding-decision-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "the real runtime is bound per spawn through the kernel configuration's tool-runtime slot — the session store constructs the kernel with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/canvas-agent/src/service/session/tools/create-runtime.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/service/session/tools/create-runtime.ts",
              "symbol": "createToolRuntime"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — and each runtime method resolves its session internally through the kernel run context, so the catalog sidecar stays a thin declaration-and-dispatch layer with no session knowledge of its own."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-agent-binding-why-14": {
      "id": "b-agent-binding-why-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "the rejected alternative was a module-level runtime the sidecar imports, which pins one session per process and drags service internals across the seam."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-agent-binding-applies-15": {
      "id": "b-agent-binding-applies-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "create-runtime.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/service/session/tools/create-runtime.ts",
              "label": "create-runtime.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — including every future runtime capability, which joins the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "LayoutToolRuntime",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " contract in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "runtime.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-agent-seam-decision-16": {
      "id": "b-agent-seam-decision-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "the catalog registers what the service defines: every descriptor — gesture or workflow call — carries its own name, label, description, and sealed parameter schema service-side under the session's tools folder, and the catalog forwards them verbatim; nothing declares tool truth on the catalog side."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-agent-seam-why-17": {
      "id": "b-agent-seam-why-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "the rejected alternative was per-tool files on the catalog side, which puts half of each tool's truth in the swappable bundle and half behind the runtime interface, making every schema change a two-file edit across the seam."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-agent-seam-applies-18": {
      "id": "b-agent-seam-applies-18",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "service/session/tools/",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/service/session/tools",
              "label": "service/session/tools/"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — including every future tool, defined service-side and forwarded."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-agent-rosters-decision-19": {
      "id": "b-agent-rosters-decision-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/canvas-agent/src/service/session/tools/operations/index.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/service/session/tools/operations/index.ts",
              "symbol": "operationTools"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/canvas-agent/src/service/session/tools/workflow/index.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/service/session/tools/workflow/index.ts",
              "symbol": "workflowTools"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " are the single sources for the surface — registration, the capabilities gesture reference, and the op ledger all derive from them — and the generated reference in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "capabilities/ops.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/catalog/layout-editor/context/capabilities/ops.ts",
              "label": "capabilities/ops.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " guards completeness both ways at import: a registered tool with no prose throws, and prose for an unregistered tool throws."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-agent-rosters-why-20": {
      "id": "b-agent-rosters-why-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "the rejected alternative was parallel rosters — a registration list, a docs list, a ledger list — which drift. A tool not in its roster is simply not on the surface, and documentation drift is a build failure rather than a lie the model reads."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-agent-rosters-applies-21": {
      "id": "b-agent-rosters-applies-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "the two roster files and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "capabilities/ops.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — including every future tool, which joins its roster and gains its prose in the same change."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-agent-order-hash-decision-22": {
      "id": "b-agent-order-hash-decision-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "registration order is pinned — the gesture roster in its own order, then the workflow roster, look first and finalize last, no duplicates — asserted by "
        },
        {
          "insert": "tool-schema-parity.test.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/test/tool-schema-parity.test.ts",
              "label": "tool-schema-parity.test.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " along with sealed root schemas and the rule that no mutator declares a viewing argument; and every eval run records a surface hash over the session tree plus the catalog's capabilities and tools directories, computed in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/eval-suite/runner/src/scenario/queue.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/eval-suite/runner/src/scenario/queue.ts",
              "symbol": "collectSourceFingerprints"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", so a surface change that skipped the prompt still reads as incomparable."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-agent-order-hash-why-23": {
      "id": "b-agent-order-hash-why-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "the rejected alternatives were treating order as cosmetic — but it is the order the model reads the surface in — and prompt-hash-only comparability, which would silently compare unlike runs. The hash is over file contents, so it also moves on a pure reorganization; that conservative answer is intended."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-agent-order-hash-applies-24": {
      "id": "b-agent-order-hash-applies-24",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "tool-schema-parity.test.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/test/tool-schema-parity.test.ts",
              "label": "tool-schema-parity.test.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "queue.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/eval-suite/runner/src/scenario/queue.ts",
              "label": "queue.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — including every future roster or surface change."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-agent-edges-decision-25": {
      "id": "b-agent-edges-decision-25",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "the harness's outward edges are one-way: "
        },
        {
          "insert": "viewer/",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/viewer",
              "label": "viewer/"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " reads the service only over its HTTP routes and nothing under "
        },
        {
          "insert": "service/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " imports the viewer; "
        },
        {
          "insert": "protocol.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/protocol.ts",
              "label": "protocol.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is types-only wire vocabulary with no runtime, pipeline, or kernel imports. The deliberate store-to-tools cycle stays safe because the tool files import the session as a type only — the store alone value-imports the runtime binding."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-agent-edges-why-26": {
      "id": "b-agent-edges-why-26",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "the rejected alternative was letting the service know about its viewer, or the sidecar construct sessions — a run would behave differently when watched, and a type-only edge turned into a value import converts a compile-time relationship into a load-order problem."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-agent-edges-applies-27": {
      "id": "b-agent-edges-applies-27",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "viewer/",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/viewer",
              "label": "viewer/"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "protocol.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/protocol.ts",
              "label": "protocol.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "service/session/",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/service/session",
              "label": "service/session/"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — including every future import across these edges: type-only stays type-only."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-agent-craft-decision-28": {
      "id": "b-agent-craft-decision-28",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "every presentation number the agent is asked to hit — node sizes and minimum width, row and column gaps, arrow corridors, section gutters, frame padding, board-area multiple and ink share — is one structured value, "
        },
        {
