        {
          "insert": ". Its exported getCanvasAuthoringGuidance function returns named topics, their rendered text, and a content fingerprint without starting a kernel. The internal agent consumes the same topics through individual context loaders. This export prepares external reuse but does not itself implement an MCP."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-agent-authoring-why": {
      "id": "b-agent-authoring-why",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Design knowledge and session behavior have separate owners. The shared topics explain visual patterns, multi-zoom composition, containment, and vocabulary. The system prompt owns core philosophy directly after purpose and depth assessment as its own phase. The prompt now applies the behavioral reference through orientate, assess_depth, understand, map_patterns, build_sections, render_validate, and finalize phases using the live state and Canvas tools at each step. Shape and color facts derive from the object-preference registry. The system prompt owns the quality checklist as success criteria. It links physical review questions to active lint rules without treating an automated pass as proof of conceptual quality."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
